immutable FP16 model and persistent cache, run F_0 and F_r with the same h_j, l_j, xi_j, and inference path, and record the full action chunks a_j0 and a_jr plus the local output discrepancy L_r. Use fake-quant/dequantized GEMM only as a profiling implementation; record whether it was used and keep it separate from the real low-bit-kernel evaluation. Output paired model traces indexed by (j,r).\n5. Execute paired environment counterfactuals. Restore the same simulator state z_j and eta_j for the two traces, apply the first executable action from each full chunk, and record o_(j+1)0, o_(j+1)r, and the simulator's independent contact/task-transition state. The downstream output of this step is the actual next observation and state transition caused by the altered action, not merely a changed intermediate discrepancy.\n6. Compute the consequence object. Calculate sigma_a from the coordinate variance of FP16 full action chunks and sigma_o from the mean per-pixel standard deviation of FP16 next observations; use named floors epsilon_a=epsilon_o=1e-3 in normalized units, with a pre-registered 1e-4/1e-3/1e-2 sensitivity check. Compute d_a and d_o as the normalized full-action-chunk and next-observation differences, set lambda_a=lambda_o=1 by default with a held-out sensitivity sweep over lambda_a/lambda_o in {0.5,1,2}, and output C_r as their episode mean with bootstrap intervals over complete episodes.\n7. Replace the local allocation operator without retraining. Set B to the exact high-precision-site count or matched bit-cost of the QuantWAMs comparison schedule, rank sites by C_r, and upgrade the top-B sites while leaving all other sites at b_lo; resolve ties by the registry order. This modifies the numerical precision assignment and therefore the downstream generated action chunk, while preserving the same checkpoint, denoising schedule, data, and model architecture.\n8. Run the confound-isolating diagnostic. On the same episodes, compare L_r and C_r using Spearman rank correlation separately on simulator-identified contact/task-transition and non-contact subsets, then compare top-B C_r allocation against top-B L_r allocation and a score-permuted negative control. The reported object is the divergence in downstream action/observation and task metrics, not a claim that a correlation itself is causal.\n9. Validate the selected schedule on held-out RoboTwin 2.0 and LIBERO episodes with the real low-bit kernel. Compare FP16, the matched local-fidelity baseline, the C_r allocation, and uniform precision at the same B; measure task success, contact-sensitive failure rate, full action-chunk deviation, next-observation deviation, peak memory, and latency, with the same Fast-WAM configuration and multiple episode seeds.\n10. Keep CPU arithmetic checks and deployment claims separate. CPU runs may verify site indexing, deterministic paired seeds, scale normalization, and C_r arithmetic only; they do not establish robot success, GPU memory, or speedup. Report any LingBot-VA replication as a separate calibration/inference experiment with its offload and checkpoint configuration, and do not combine fake-quant traces with real-kernel performance.",
